[#:seon.task{:name "a-merge-is-keyed-by-the-assignment"
             :kind :function
             :intent "(hybrid-done-and-merge M6) The merge is keyed by the assignment (`:seon.task/assignment`, the entity `seon.task/attempt-tx` writes). Namespace `seon.cluster.squash` becomes `seon.merge` (requirers `seon.cluster.agent`, `seon.task`, `script/astra_cost_handoff.clj`, three tests); `seon.merge/merge!` folds `seon.cluster.source/land!` and `land-held!`; `prepare-merge!` and `accept-merge!` take the assignment and its source commit C; `seon.task/close!` writes `:seon.task/outcome` on the assignment; `my.root/merge!`, `merge-requests` and `close!` key by `:seon.task/assignment`; `seon.context` and `seon.cluster.message` offer `my.root/merge!` with the assignment. `seon.cluster.source/land!` stays one line calling `seon.merge/merge!` until M8. Task ids derive from the namespace: `resources/seon/tasks/seon.cluster.squash.edn` becomes `seon.merge.edn` (its entries M2, M3a, M4 and the later M7, M9, M11 included) and the `:seon/tasks` tags in `squash_test` follow; the symbol is converted in the task files `seon.fault`, `seon.program`, `seon.cluster.agent`, `seon.cluster.source`, `seon.flow`, `seon.turn.world` and `docs/seon/architecture/vocabulary.md` in the same commit. Red proof: `my.root-test/a-merge-is-keyed-by-the-assignment` (`(my.root/merge! {:seon.task/assignment k})` on a done branch gives :seon.task/outcome :merged, `:seon.task/merge-base` = C, `:seon.task/merge-commit` present; `(my.root/merge-requests)` lists open assignments with their unmerged coordinates). Cost: merge of one function with reused gate results under 1 s."
             :must-read #{my.root/merge! my.root/merge-requests my.root/close! seon.cluster.source/land! seon.cluster.source/land-held! seon.cluster.source/accept-merge! seon.cluster.source/merge-base seon.task/close! seon.task/attempt-tx seon.context/current-state}
             :needs #{[:seon.task/sym seon.flow/an-ended-attempt-reaches-main-in-one-transaction-and-its-branch-is-deleted]}
             :evidence #{"docs/research/agent-platform/2026-10-12/hybrid-done-and-merge.md"}}]
